course: dictionary
lesson: 14515
title: Perceived: noticed, and how things seem
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Perceive means to notice something with your senses, such as seeing, hearing or feeling it, or to understand it in a certain way. Perceived is its past form, so it can mean "noticed" or "thought of".
explain: «The cat perceived a mouse under the bush.» The cat noticed the mouse by seeing or hearing it. When you meet an unknown word, ask what the base word means and whether the ending changes the meaning.
explain: «She was perceived as kind by the whole class.» Here perceived means the class thought of her as kind. Perceived can also be an adjective: «a perceived danger» is a danger people believe is there, even if it is not really there.
fact: Perceive means to notice or understand something through your senses.
fact: «Perceived» can mean noticed, or thought of in a certain way.
fact: «A perceived danger» means something believed to be dangerous, though it may not be real.
fact: Phrases such as «perceived as» and «widely perceived» show how people think of someone or something.
fact: In science, what is perceived is what our senses notice, so it is not always the whole truth.
exercise: «The dog perceived a noise at the door and barked.» What does perceived mean here? | Forgot the noise completely | *Noticed the noise by hearing it | Bought a new door | Made the noise itself
exercise: «The teacher was perceived as strict, but she was really very fair.» What does this tell you? | The teacher was tired and cross | The teacher had never met the class | The teacher was strict in every single lesson | *Other people thought of the teacher as strict
exercise: «Ben felt a perceived danger in the dark wood, but there was no danger at all.» What is a perceived danger? | A danger that is certain and very near | A kind of tree found in woods | *A danger people believe is there, though it is not real | A friendly animal that lives in the dark
test: «The owl perceived the mouse moving in the grass.» What does perceived mean? | Forgot all about it | Ate it straight away | *Noticed by seeing it | Hid from it under a log
test: Which phrase shows how people think of something? | Sat on a chair | *Widely perceived as | Very loud noise | Ran away quickly
exam: What does «a perceived threat» most likely mean? | *A threat people believe is there, though it may not be real | A threat that everyone has forgotten | A threat that is real and certain | A threat that has been sent by post
